      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ZENITH STRIDE (8) has finished fourth in stronger company in both outings since a fresh win here. Tactics will be crucial from the wide draw but this is a nice drop in grade so he is in the right race to return to winning form. G O A T (6) was well beaten in stronger company at his latest appearance but was good when runner-up here prior so is better placed and should be approaching peak fitness now. CHIEF RUNNINGCLOUD (4) overcame a 40m handicap to win at this circuit and distance last time and led from out wide when placed prior. Can continue the strong form. VALTINO (10) starts from the extreme outside but was good when he came from a 40m handicap and raced three wide wide without cover for a close second at this circuit and distance. CALL ME JACK (1) bombed standing start last time so is much better off behind a mobile having won here two back and gets the ace draw.",
